    "updated_at": "2025-01-15T07:15:00Z",
    "body": "> I believe another fix would be to use the DOM manipulation task source in \"Try to scroll to the fragment\", to ensure that the task it queues runs before the task that fires the load event.\n\nUsing try to scroll the fragment doesn't sound right to me, since it checks parser state, the parser may have stopped running by that point, so the \"stopped parsing\" step of that function would need to change:\n\n> If document has no parser, or its parser has [stopped parsing](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#stop-parsing),",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
