    "created_at": "2025-01-17T01:05:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-01-17T01:05:37Z",
    "body": "Right, that's why the current spec has a model which polls periodically and gives up in an implementation-defined manner (usually when the user starts scrolling).\n\nI think the standard's current model is good in that regard. But the OP points out that due to the timing of our call into that algorithm, it's currently *prohibited* from having `:target` match _earlier_ than a certain point. That is worth fixing, if there are indeed some browsers in which it matches earlier.",
