    "created_at": "2025-01-17T08:21:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-01-17T08:21:44Z",
    "body": "I think so, but I now also think some of the conditions in \"try to scroll to the fragment\" might still be applicable. If the end user has started scrolling we'd still not want to scroll.\n\nAnd we'd need a way to cancel the \"try to scroll to the fragment\" steps I think to account for this new condition.\n\nNow then there's still the question as to whether implementations adhere to this or if they also sometimes scroll after the parser has stopped. So for testing we probably want:\n\n- Early target in the document, but getting to `DOMContentLoaded` takes long.\n- Late target in the document or document essentially fits in a packet.\n- Target is inserted post-parsing.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
